1
00:00:02,360 --> 00:00:10,910
Lesson 24. Amber writes a song. Ted always writes the songs for the rock band, but now Amber

2
00:00:10,759 --> 00:00:16,709
says she wants to start writing songs too. She sings him the first lines of her new song.

3
00:00:17,660 --> 00:00:23,509
Ted, you know how all along you've been in charge of all the lyrics for our band?

4
00:00:23,359 --> 00:00:26,429
That's right Amber. Everybody loves my songs.

5
00:00:27,140 --> 00:00:30,929
Well, I hope they'll love my songs too.

6
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:32,570
But you don't write songs.

7
00:00:33,579 --> 00:00:41,549
I'm sick and tired of singing your songs all the time. I want to sing my own songs.

8
00:00:42,079 --> 00:00:46,809
Okay, no need to freak out. First things first. Have you written a song yet?

9
00:00:47,460 --> 00:00:51,369
Yes. As a matter of fact, I have.

10
00:00:51,219 --> 00:00:53,109
Well, let's hear it then.

11
00:00:55,040 --> 00:00:58,509
Okay, but it's still a work in progress.

12
00:00:58,880 --> 00:01:01,509
Stop trying to buy time. Let's hear the song.

13
00:01:03,179 --> 00:01:13,350
My boyfriend is crazy. Crazy about baking cookies. I know for sure that there is no cure.

14
00:01:13,579 --> 00:01:16,510
Cut it out. Stop teasing me. I am cured.

15
00:01:16,980 --> 00:01:18,050
All better?

16
00:01:18,280 --> 00:01:24,670
Yes. I'll never bake another cookie again. My parents made a fortune. Now we can all just chill out.

